WEBVTT

00:26.776 --> 00:29.988
-Is it around here?
-Yes, we'll be there soon.

00:30.071 --> 00:31.156
Is this it?

00:32.490 --> 00:34.868
All right, let's get our money's worth!

00:37.787 --> 00:39.456
ETHNIC CAFE

00:47.046 --> 00:48.339
This is good stuff.

00:48.423 --> 00:50.008
It's great, isn't it?

00:53.344 --> 00:55.513
Do you not like ethnic food?

00:58.099 --> 01:00.435
Come on, you should have just told me.

01:00.518 --> 01:04.355
Well, every single option
you gave me, Dr. Matsubara,

01:04.439 --> 01:06.274
was ethnic food.

01:06.357 --> 01:08.693
I hate people
who just try and read the room.

01:08.777 --> 01:09.944
Sorry.

01:10.028 --> 01:13.364
But this feeling of the spices
rushing through your whole body

01:13.448 --> 01:14.991
is the absolute best.

01:16.701 --> 01:21.581
Whether a person reads the room or not
won't show up in an autopsy, will it?

01:22.540 --> 01:25.502
If you die, nobody is going to
know your were kind.

01:26.127 --> 01:27.337
I wouldn't want that.

01:29.798 --> 01:30.799
Right…

01:30.882 --> 01:33.343
MOM: YOUR SISTER IS IN TROUBLE

01:36.971 --> 01:39.557
YOUR SISTER IS IN TROUBLE

01:39.641 --> 01:46.773
PARLIAMENT MEMBER TOSHIO AOTA'S
FORBIDDEN AFFAIR: HIS CHIEF SECRETARY!

02:02.831 --> 02:03.665
CONTACTS

02:03.748 --> 02:06.876
SAKI MATSUBARA

02:14.509 --> 02:18.179
OFFICE OF TOSHIO AOTA

03:11.107 --> 03:12.108
Dr. Matsubara?

03:12.692 --> 03:13.526
Yes?

03:13.610 --> 03:15.069
Do you need any help?

03:15.695 --> 03:17.864
No, I'm fine.

03:20.783 --> 03:23.411
Hello, this is Medical Examiner Japan.

03:25.705 --> 03:26.664
What?

03:27.165 --> 03:29.334
The parliament member's office?

03:30.543 --> 03:31.711
Yes.

03:32.962 --> 03:34.005
I understand.

03:40.094 --> 03:41.221
Hello.

03:41.888 --> 03:45.016
The deceased is Toshio Aota,
a lawmaker from the National Party.

03:45.099 --> 03:48.436
When his chief secretary, Saki Matsubara,
visited the office this morning,

03:48.519 --> 03:51.606
he was discovered already hanging.

03:52.190 --> 03:54.817
No suicide note has been found,

03:54.901 --> 03:57.695
but a magazine published an article
about an affair of his.

03:57.779 --> 04:01.157
Furthermore, it was with the person who
first discovered him, Saki Matsubara.

04:01.241 --> 04:04.494
Considering the situation,
the police are viewing it as a suicide.

04:06.412 --> 04:07.247
Wait.

04:07.330 --> 04:09.332
Where's Ms. Dojima?

04:09.999 --> 04:12.835
She was called in by the chief
regarding this case.

04:15.255 --> 04:16.256
Dojima.

04:16.756 --> 04:19.717
Don't look too hard into
the parliament member's death.

04:20.885 --> 04:22.178
You get it, right?

04:27.141 --> 04:28.977
No subcutaneous bleeding.

04:29.060 --> 04:31.187
No facial congestion either.

04:31.271 --> 04:35.275
The stop of circulation
is highly likely due to pressure.

04:35.858 --> 04:36.901
Which means?

04:36.985 --> 04:40.280
There is a possibility
that he was hanged after he died.

04:41.239 --> 04:45.576
I see multiple small,
hole-like wounds on his chest.

04:48.621 --> 04:51.082
The autopsy shows, as expected,

04:51.165 --> 04:56.129
Mr. Aota's cause of death
was not asphyxiation from hanging.

04:56.212 --> 04:59.424
The discoloration on Mr. Aota's
body is concentrated on his back.

04:59.507 --> 05:02.427
If he had died from hanging,

05:02.510 --> 05:06.139
it should have appeared
on his fingers and lower legs.

05:06.222 --> 05:07.265
It doesn't add up.

05:07.348 --> 05:10.310
Does that mean it was murder?

05:10.393 --> 05:15.857
Mr. Aota appears to have suffered
cardiac arrest before he was hanged.

05:15.940 --> 05:20.194
It seems someone used a rope
to hang him several hours after his death.

05:21.529 --> 05:24.490
There are minor scrapes
and bruises on his hands and feet,

05:24.574 --> 05:26.326
but they are all light injuries.

05:26.409 --> 05:27.660
From their location,

05:27.744 --> 05:30.330
they are highly likely
from a fall or a stumble.

05:30.413 --> 05:32.457
Was that fall the cause of death?

05:33.916 --> 05:36.753
There was a mark indicating
a strong impact to the chest.

05:36.836 --> 05:40.798
The shock most likely fractured his ribs,
which punctured his lung.

05:40.882 --> 05:43.092
We also confirmed
bleeding inside the chest,

05:43.176 --> 05:45.803
but nothing that we could say
is the cause of death.

05:45.887 --> 05:50.224
There were also
four small stab wounds on the chest.

05:50.308 --> 05:52.810
Rather than stab wounds from a knife,

05:52.894 --> 05:57.190
it looks more like a mark left by
forcing something sharp into the skin.

05:58.191 --> 06:01.694
There is almost no bleeding
from the wounds, which means

06:01.778 --> 06:04.822
it is highly likely these wounds
were inflicted after death.

06:04.906 --> 06:10.078
Meaning, whoever made those wounds
holds the key to this case?

06:17.627 --> 06:19.378
For now,

06:19.462 --> 06:20.630
it's a mystery.

06:25.176 --> 06:27.428
Apparently, that man Aota,
whom we autopsied today,

06:27.512 --> 06:29.388
was suspected of having an affair.

06:29.472 --> 06:31.766
What? Really?

06:31.849 --> 06:35.311
And it was with his chief secretary
who first found him.

06:35.978 --> 06:38.773
Maybe she killed him over a messy affair.

06:42.568 --> 06:44.195
What do you think, Dr. Matsubara?

06:49.200 --> 06:52.245
That's… my older sister.

06:53.871 --> 06:55.039
-Huh?
-What?

06:55.123 --> 06:57.333
That politician's secretary,
Saki Matsubara.

06:58.251 --> 06:59.710
She's my older sister.

07:06.801 --> 07:10.096
Please let me join the investigation
for this case.

07:11.389 --> 07:13.307
I can't accept this,

07:13.391 --> 07:15.059
so I want to investigate it myself.

07:17.186 --> 07:18.396
Please.

07:30.199 --> 07:31.868
I think

07:32.952 --> 07:34.495
this could be

07:35.079 --> 07:39.500
a piece of a bigger puzzle.

07:44.755 --> 07:46.507
Hello, this is Medical Examiner…

07:48.843 --> 07:49.677
What?

07:51.804 --> 07:52.638
Yes.

07:52.722 --> 07:53.723
That's right.

07:55.766 --> 07:56.851
Yes.

07:59.103 --> 08:00.771
Yes, goodbye.

08:04.025 --> 08:05.485
Is something wrong?

08:06.486 --> 08:11.908
The MHLW told me not to get involved
in the investigation of this case.

08:38.518 --> 08:39.727
I…

08:40.937 --> 08:43.147
was having an affair with Mr. Aota.

08:46.359 --> 08:47.860
We met at my apartment

08:48.861 --> 08:50.863
during the day of the incident.

08:51.614 --> 08:54.283
I seriously can't believe you.
Do you think I'm stupid?

08:54.367 --> 08:59.455
He told me he would divorce his wife,
but he never actually did it.

08:59.539 --> 09:02.875
Recently, we ended up arguing
every time we met.

09:12.843 --> 09:14.095
But I never imagined

09:15.721 --> 09:16.973
he would commit suicide.

09:17.056 --> 09:20.851
We are investigating with
the possibility of murder in mind as well.

09:22.562 --> 09:23.729
Is that so?

09:24.647 --> 09:31.112
Mr. Aota fell from the exterior staircase
of the apartment where you live?

09:31.696 --> 09:32.613
Yes.

09:34.156 --> 09:36.450
May we investigate that?

09:38.202 --> 09:39.078
Go ahead.

09:41.163 --> 09:45.084
No bloodstains or signs of a fall
were found on the apartment stairs.

09:45.167 --> 09:49.005
Aota did not appear
on any of the security cameras either.

09:49.088 --> 09:51.132
The components found in the wound

09:51.215 --> 09:54.218
did not match the concrete components
of the apartment stairs.

09:57.388 --> 10:00.099
None of it adds up.

10:01.601 --> 10:03.394
But that makes no sense.

10:03.477 --> 10:05.271
Why would she come forward

10:05.354 --> 10:07.690
just to lie to us
and seem more suspicious?

10:08.232 --> 10:10.109
There must be a reason.

10:12.445 --> 10:14.155
Dr. Matsubara,

10:14.238 --> 10:16.616
do you have any insights?

10:20.453 --> 10:22.413
She has always been like that.

10:22.496 --> 10:27.668
She just reads the room
and tries to please everyone.

10:28.502 --> 10:31.797
Her special talent was avoiding conflict.

10:33.883 --> 10:34.967
An affair?

10:36.093 --> 10:37.178
Murder?

10:38.721 --> 10:39.889
That's hilarious.

10:39.972 --> 10:41.599
That's a lot of conflict.

10:48.564 --> 10:50.733
She might actually be…

10:51.734 --> 10:53.235
reading the room right now.

10:54.945 --> 11:00.284
So Saki Matsubara knows the truth
that Aota fell somewhere else,

11:00.368 --> 11:06.957
and she is lying
to try and hide another truth?

11:08.292 --> 11:10.586
It is only a possibility.

11:10.670 --> 11:12.963
Did you find anything out
about the stab wounds?

11:13.047 --> 11:15.424
There is something strange
about the entry paths.

11:15.508 --> 11:16.675
Strange?

11:17.468 --> 11:19.178
Out of the four wounds,

11:19.261 --> 11:21.639
three are very shallow,

11:21.722 --> 11:25.226
but the fourth one goes
all the way into the chest cavity.

11:25.309 --> 11:27.103
Furthermore, all the wounds

11:27.186 --> 11:30.439
were deliberately inflicted
along a path that avoids the ribs.

11:31.273 --> 11:32.775
Any trace substances yet?

11:32.858 --> 11:34.985
We should get results soon. I'll check.

11:46.455 --> 11:49.417
PARLIAMENT MEMBER AOTA (50)
FOUND HANGED IN OFFICE

12:02.638 --> 12:04.181
Thank you.

12:04.265 --> 12:05.099
Sure.

12:05.182 --> 12:06.016
Let's eat.

12:06.100 --> 12:07.476
Let's eat.

12:12.022 --> 12:14.316
It's rare to see you working this late.

12:15.818 --> 12:19.613
Apparently, Aota used to work
as a surgeon at Senshu Hospital.

12:20.156 --> 12:23.075
I might find something out,
so I plan to go there tomorrow.

12:31.750 --> 12:35.087
I summarized the policies
Aota was working on.

12:35.171 --> 12:39.175
It looks like he was recently drafting
a bill related to the healthcare system.

12:40.676 --> 12:42.428
Impressive.

12:43.471 --> 12:45.514
This is about all I can do right now.

12:50.227 --> 12:52.021
I really don't like her.

12:52.646 --> 12:53.481
My sister.

12:57.735 --> 13:01.322
She always reads the room
and tries to smooth everything over.

13:02.823 --> 13:05.326
When she’s in trouble,
she takes it all on herself.

13:06.952 --> 13:10.748
She acts tough and says she's fine
even when she isn't.

13:10.831 --> 13:12.374
It's all so annoying.

13:15.711 --> 13:16.629
But…

13:17.588 --> 13:20.841
my sister would never do
anything to hurt another person.

13:21.675 --> 13:23.761
An affair? Murder?

13:24.303 --> 13:26.263
Why would she lie?

13:38.817 --> 13:43.030
That means it's your turn to step in,
Dr. Matsubara.

13:47.076 --> 13:51.247
Living people might tell lies sometimes.

13:52.456 --> 13:55.292
But bodies never do.

13:58.379 --> 14:02.424
The truth is there, I'm sure.

14:08.514 --> 14:10.432
Our food will get cold. Let's eat.

14:19.108 --> 14:20.025
Thank you.

14:20.109 --> 14:20.943
Goodbye.

14:21.026 --> 14:21.902
Goodbye.

14:23.320 --> 14:24.321
Mom.

14:24.905 --> 14:25.781
Are you okay?

14:27.032 --> 14:29.618
Isn't that Mr. Aota's wife?

14:38.043 --> 14:40.588
Is your mother hospitalized?

14:41.255 --> 14:42.214
Yes.

14:42.298 --> 14:45.009
Her lungs have always been a bit weak.

14:46.135 --> 14:47.177
I'm sorry.

14:47.261 --> 14:50.264
We've been going around
asking questions about Mr. Aota.

14:51.098 --> 14:52.725
Did you find out anything?

14:53.767 --> 14:54.727
No.

14:59.481 --> 15:00.482
Hey.

15:00.566 --> 15:02.776
That's the chairman
of the Senshu Group, isn't it?

15:05.487 --> 15:08.198
A charismatic figure
in the medical world who believes

15:08.282 --> 15:09.575
in saving every life.

15:10.743 --> 15:13.913
My husband originally
started working at this hospital

15:13.996 --> 15:16.040
because he admired Chairman Mukai.

15:16.874 --> 15:20.002
Ten years ago, he suddenly
decided to become a politician.

15:20.085 --> 15:23.213
All of Mr. Aota's policies were wonderful.

15:23.297 --> 15:26.675
Or like, they felt created
by a proper human being.

15:30.512 --> 15:31.347
I'm sorry.

15:35.768 --> 15:36.936
On that day,

15:38.729 --> 15:41.148
he told me he would be late,

15:41.899 --> 15:46.487
but would come home early the next day
so we could go out for dinner somewhere.

15:51.241 --> 15:52.201
But…

15:53.410 --> 15:55.704
that day turned out to be his last.

16:01.251 --> 16:02.169
TOSHIO AOTA

16:02.252 --> 16:03.420
May I have a balloon?

16:03.504 --> 16:04.880
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

16:04.964 --> 16:07.049
You're welcome. Bye-bye!

16:11.345 --> 16:13.430
May I have one?

16:13.514 --> 16:14.348
Sure.

16:14.431 --> 16:15.391
Thank you.

16:15.474 --> 16:16.767
Doctor, is that…

16:17.351 --> 16:18.769
The reason balloons float

16:18.852 --> 16:21.772
is because the helium inside it
is lighter than the air around--

16:25.067 --> 16:26.193
It's okay.

16:26.860 --> 16:27.695
Take this one.

16:36.453 --> 16:37.413
It's okay.

16:37.496 --> 16:38.706
Have this one.

16:41.041 --> 16:42.626
Thank you very much.

16:42.710 --> 16:44.670
Thank you!

16:44.753 --> 16:45.879
Let's go.

16:52.720 --> 16:54.013
Excuse me.

16:54.096 --> 16:55.180
One more?

16:56.849 --> 16:58.100
One more, please.

16:58.183 --> 16:59.101
Oh, sure.

16:59.184 --> 17:00.436
Thank you, sorry.

17:00.519 --> 17:01.437
Thank you.

17:04.023 --> 17:05.107
Sorry.

17:12.406 --> 17:14.867
When you listen
to the stories of the living,

17:15.409 --> 17:18.245
the truth becomes harder to know.

17:21.874 --> 17:23.417
Dr. Masumi.

17:23.500 --> 17:26.628
Do you ever read the room?

17:30.132 --> 17:34.219
The human brain contains nerve cells
called mirror neurons.

17:34.303 --> 17:37.598
These are brain cells that react
to actions of others

17:37.681 --> 17:40.100
by mirroring what we observe.

17:40.934 --> 17:42.394
Because of this function,

17:42.478 --> 17:46.023
we are naturally wired to empathize
with the words and actions of others.

17:51.904 --> 17:52.821
What is it?

17:54.573 --> 17:56.158
I just read the room.

17:57.785 --> 17:58.952
So you can read it?

17:59.536 --> 18:01.580
It's simply the function of nerve cells.

18:02.581 --> 18:03.957
Is that how it works?

18:13.258 --> 18:15.594
I don't think it's a bad thing.

18:18.722 --> 18:23.852
Reading the room
is an innate ability humans possess.

18:23.936 --> 18:26.563
It is one of our tools for survival.

18:49.461 --> 18:51.296
Take a seat wherever.

18:57.094 --> 18:59.513
You didn't engage in an affair, right?

19:00.389 --> 19:02.641
You read the weekly magazines, didn't you?

19:02.724 --> 19:03.934
They're lying.

19:04.017 --> 19:05.227
They're not.

19:05.769 --> 19:06.603
Why?

19:09.898 --> 19:11.358
Answer my question.

19:12.734 --> 19:14.695
There is no particular reason.

19:14.778 --> 19:16.780
I just fell in love with him, that's all.

19:16.864 --> 19:18.991
But what you said
about the stairs was a lie.

19:24.997 --> 19:26.290
You didn't kill him, right?

19:28.709 --> 19:29.835
Hey.

19:29.918 --> 19:31.461
What are you trying to protect?

19:31.545 --> 19:33.213
Is it really that important to you?

19:33.297 --> 19:34.923
Is it worth more than your own life?

19:35.007 --> 19:35.966
Shut up!

19:37.718 --> 19:40.304
Don't assume everyone
can live their life like you do.

19:41.805 --> 19:42.723
What?

19:43.891 --> 19:45.267
What does that mean?

19:46.059 --> 19:48.437
Suzune, you've always been this way.

19:48.520 --> 19:51.356
You think speaking the truth
makes you entirely right.

19:52.649 --> 19:55.903
I have spent my whole life living
in a world that isn't quite so simple.

19:58.113 --> 20:01.617
A world like that
is completely meaningless.

20:06.163 --> 20:07.581
Just leave.

20:14.296 --> 20:15.130
Fine.

20:16.590 --> 20:18.592
But answer me just one last thing.

20:19.176 --> 20:20.093
What?

20:20.594 --> 20:24.056
Did you truly love Aota?

20:24.139 --> 20:25.641
What kind of question is that?

20:26.225 --> 20:29.853
Did you genuinely intend
to build a life together with Aota?

20:38.570 --> 20:39.738
Yes, I did.

20:42.741 --> 20:43.742
See?

20:44.493 --> 20:45.452
Are we done now?

20:46.370 --> 20:47.454
Leave.

20:58.674 --> 21:02.970
These are the chemical components
from Aota's clothing and nasal cavity.

21:04.137 --> 21:07.891
The amount of volatile sulfur compounds
is exceptionally high.

21:08.392 --> 21:09.434
Yes.

21:09.518 --> 21:11.311
I can't quite figure out this part.

21:11.395 --> 21:14.564
We also recovered traces
of phthalocyanine pigments,

21:14.648 --> 21:17.609
glycerol, emulsifiers, and fragrance
from the stab wounds.

21:17.693 --> 21:19.611
Phthalocyanine is a pigment, isn't it?

21:19.695 --> 21:21.446
The kind used in paints and inks.

21:21.530 --> 21:24.032
Glycerol is commonly used
as a solvent in ink as well.

21:24.116 --> 21:26.827
Emulsifiers and fragrances
point toward cosmetics.

21:32.457 --> 21:33.834
It's a mystery.

21:36.753 --> 21:38.338
I need to look into something.

21:40.090 --> 21:41.174
What?

21:42.509 --> 21:46.305
There might be a piece of the puzzle
we've missed.

21:53.770 --> 21:55.314
CHEMICAL COMPOUNDS

22:15.000 --> 22:17.836
This… might be the secret spice.

22:19.463 --> 22:21.381
The secret spice?

22:21.465 --> 22:22.924
Asafoetida.

22:23.008 --> 22:25.093
Otherwise known as the secret spice.

22:26.094 --> 22:27.721
It is native to South Africa

22:27.804 --> 22:31.308
and has a vey strong odor,
much like garlic or durian.

22:35.270 --> 22:37.355
The chemical composition is a close match.

22:37.439 --> 22:40.233
When heated in oil,
it volatilizes quickly,

22:40.317 --> 22:43.612
which explains how microparticles
could adhere to someone.

22:43.695 --> 22:46.031
Incredible, Dr. Matsubara!

22:46.114 --> 22:47.365
Ethnic maniac!

22:48.784 --> 22:52.370
This feeling of the spices
rushing through your whole body

22:52.454 --> 22:54.247
is the absolute best.

22:54.748 --> 22:55.832
SECRET SPICE CURRY

22:57.626 --> 22:59.002
I need to go verify this.

22:59.586 --> 23:00.420
What?

23:01.004 --> 23:03.173
Don't tell me you're leaving too?

23:03.757 --> 23:07.385
There might be a piece of the puzzle
we've missed.

23:07.886 --> 23:10.806
We are indeed using it
in our current special menu, but…

23:11.389 --> 23:14.935
Did you happen to hear anything heavy
falling nearby on that day?

23:15.018 --> 23:17.395
Oh, I'm not sure…

23:42.129 --> 23:44.005
EMERGENCY LADDER

24:13.326 --> 24:16.913
That day, Aota fell down the stairs
at the Sanyo Hotel.

24:16.997 --> 24:19.499
I believe he took a heavy hit
to his chest after falling.

24:19.583 --> 24:21.042
If that's the case,

24:21.126 --> 24:22.919
then he really did die from a fall, right?

24:23.003 --> 24:26.131
But we still don't understand
the mystery of the stab wound.

24:36.266 --> 24:39.519
Like a mark left by forcing
something sharp into the skin.

24:39.603 --> 24:41.188
I was having an affair with Toshio Aota.

24:41.271 --> 24:43.356
I believe he took a heavy hit
to his chest after falling.

24:43.440 --> 24:46.526
We also recovered traces of phthalocyanine
pigments from the stab wounds.

24:46.610 --> 24:48.320
The kind used in paints and inks.

24:48.403 --> 24:50.238
Her lungs have always been a bit weak.

24:50.322 --> 24:51.907
She just reads the room…

24:59.998 --> 25:01.374
The pieces might be…

25:02.417 --> 25:03.960
coming together.

25:10.800 --> 25:11.635
First,

25:11.718 --> 25:13.803
regarding Aota's cause of death,

25:14.387 --> 25:16.348
a certain hypothesis has been formed.

25:17.557 --> 25:21.937
Traces of a rare spice called asafoetida
have been detected

25:22.020 --> 25:25.649
on the clothing Aota wore
and in his nasal cavity.

25:26.524 --> 25:28.193
On the day Aota died,

25:28.276 --> 25:32.239
a dish using this spice
was being served at the Sanyo Hotel.

25:32.322 --> 25:35.033
And, Aota's fingerprints and bloodstains

25:35.116 --> 25:37.535
were detected
on the hotel's external stairs.

25:38.286 --> 25:39.537
It is likely that,

25:39.621 --> 25:42.707
somehow, Aota fell from
these stairs and hit his chest hard,

25:42.791 --> 25:45.669
fracturing his ribs,
causing a hole to open in his lungs.

25:46.753 --> 25:50.674
When a hole opens in the lung,
air leaks into the chest cavity,

25:50.757 --> 25:52.842
putting pressure on the lung and heart.

25:52.926 --> 25:56.137
This condition is called
a tension pneumothorax.

25:56.221 --> 25:58.807
Judging from
the circumstances of the fall,

25:58.890 --> 26:02.185
it would not be surprising if Aota
had developed tension pneumothorax.

26:02.269 --> 26:05.647
However, during the autopsy,
we found no air to be trapped there.

26:05.730 --> 26:10.110
A tension pneumothorax
is a life-threatening, critical condition.

26:10.193 --> 26:11.653
As an emergency measure,

26:11.736 --> 26:15.782
you must puncture the chest cavity,
before it becomes fatal.

26:17.784 --> 26:18.868
What is it?

26:20.537 --> 26:23.331
Could you stab that into the chest cavity?

26:23.832 --> 26:25.041
The chest cavity?

26:26.001 --> 26:28.253
As a rough guide, it's around here.

26:28.336 --> 26:31.047
To be exact, it's between the ribs.

26:31.923 --> 26:33.883
No, no way I could do that.

26:45.353 --> 26:46.354
Could you do it?

26:53.069 --> 26:57.699
Traces of what is believed to be
ink pigments were detected in the wounds.

26:57.782 --> 26:59.284
And in his office,

26:59.367 --> 27:03.872
parts of a ballpoint pen with ink
components that match were found.

27:03.955 --> 27:05.332
If someone,

27:05.415 --> 27:07.208
as a life-saving measure for Aota,

27:07.292 --> 27:09.461
who was suffering
from a tension pneumothorax,

27:09.544 --> 27:11.671
had stabbed a ballpoint pen into him,

27:11.755 --> 27:16.176
and if that procedure
had relieved the tension pneumothorax,

27:16.801 --> 27:19.262
it would be difficult
to notice it during an autopsy.

27:25.143 --> 27:29.647
Aota's chest wound
was not a trace of an attempt to kill him.

27:29.731 --> 27:36.071
I believe it is a sign of an effort
to save his life.

27:43.411 --> 27:44.996
For Mr. Aota's sake as well,

27:46.206 --> 27:47.791
won't you please

27:48.958 --> 27:50.835
tell us the truth?

28:05.100 --> 28:06.267
I'm sorry.

28:11.356 --> 28:12.607
I'm sorry.

28:13.608 --> 28:16.444
A long time ago,
when I was walking with my mother…

28:16.528 --> 28:17.737
Mom, what's wrong?

28:17.821 --> 28:21.574
She suddenly clutched her chest
and collapsed.

28:21.658 --> 28:22.867
Are you okay?

28:22.951 --> 28:24.494
Mom, are you okay?

28:25.787 --> 28:27.038
I'm a doctor.

28:35.797 --> 28:38.258
She is experiencing
a tension pneumothorax.

28:38.341 --> 28:39.968
I have performed emergency first aid.

28:40.051 --> 28:42.595
I'm sorry, but please rest assured.

28:44.431 --> 28:46.599
-Thank you so much.
-Call an ambulance.

28:47.767 --> 28:52.605
We had been married
and together for so many years…

28:54.441 --> 28:56.985
and I thought I knew everything about him.

28:58.319 --> 28:59.696
But lately,

29:00.280 --> 29:02.699
he seemed to be hiding something.

29:04.909 --> 29:07.162
That's why, on that day,

29:07.829 --> 29:11.207
I really suspected
he was having an affair.

29:16.379 --> 29:17.422
Mr. Kakei!

29:22.510 --> 29:24.053
Do you have a moment?

29:24.554 --> 29:25.847
Not in here.

29:25.930 --> 29:27.348
Let's go somewhere else.

29:34.814 --> 29:37.567
Please retract that article.

29:38.985 --> 29:41.780
It's because you guys
are sneaking around snooping.

29:43.656 --> 29:45.784
Bribery is a crime.

29:50.497 --> 29:54.793
You're an adult,
so read the room a little bit more.

29:55.835 --> 29:56.920
Besides,

29:57.629 --> 29:59.839
an evil that can bring change

30:00.673 --> 30:04.093
is far better than justice
that can't change anything, isn't it?

30:13.645 --> 30:14.854
Mr. Aota!

30:16.189 --> 30:17.315
Follow him!

30:18.900 --> 30:19.901
Okay!

30:25.698 --> 30:26.699
Dear!

30:26.783 --> 30:27.909
Are you all right?

30:27.992 --> 30:29.118
Kaede?

30:29.619 --> 30:30.829
OFFICE OF TOSHIO AOTA

30:30.912 --> 30:32.330
Explain to me what happened.

30:34.249 --> 30:35.458
I'm sorry.

30:37.377 --> 30:38.378
Let's separate.

30:38.962 --> 30:39.796
What?

30:39.879 --> 30:41.881
It's better if we aren't together.

30:42.924 --> 30:45.134
Kaede, pretend you didn't know anything.

30:46.553 --> 30:47.887
Live a normal life.

30:49.180 --> 30:50.723
What are you saying?

30:52.225 --> 30:53.434
I don't understand!

31:00.400 --> 31:01.526
Dear?

31:03.862 --> 31:05.154
Dear!

31:08.074 --> 31:09.158
Dear!

31:09.742 --> 31:11.119
Dear!

31:11.202 --> 31:12.245
Dear!

31:12.328 --> 31:14.539
Dear! Are you okay? What's wrong?

31:17.166 --> 31:18.543
What?

31:37.687 --> 31:39.063
Dear!

31:39.147 --> 31:40.398
It's not working!

31:42.901 --> 31:45.111
Dear! Don't go!

32:00.919 --> 32:02.879
Dear?

32:05.381 --> 32:06.549
Dear…

32:07.300 --> 32:08.551
Why?

32:10.094 --> 32:11.804
Dear!

32:19.729 --> 32:21.022
I…

32:22.231 --> 32:24.484
killed my husband, didn't I?

32:25.485 --> 32:27.570
Out of the four stab wounds,

32:28.279 --> 32:31.824
one of them successfully punctured
his chest cavity

32:31.908 --> 32:34.327
and allowed air to escape.

32:36.037 --> 32:37.080
However,

32:37.789 --> 32:39.749
by that point,

32:40.667 --> 32:42.543
your husband had already passed.

32:47.632 --> 32:48.967
The traces…

32:50.843 --> 32:52.553
of your attempts to save him…

32:54.639 --> 32:56.474
told us the truth.

33:00.645 --> 33:03.022
I believe your husband

33:04.649 --> 33:06.484
was trying his best

33:06.567 --> 33:09.404
to stay alive as long as he could
for your sake.

33:28.006 --> 33:31.217
I never had an affair with him.

33:33.428 --> 33:34.679
Mr. Aota…

33:37.974 --> 33:39.225
Mr. Aota…

33:42.937 --> 33:46.983
was trying to expose
the bribery between Mr. Kakei

33:48.860 --> 33:50.945
and the Senshu Group.

33:55.658 --> 33:57.869
It was about a month ago

33:58.828 --> 34:02.206
when Mr. Aota realized that Chairman Mukai
of the Senshu Group

34:02.957 --> 34:05.084
was giving bribes to Kakei.

34:05.168 --> 34:06.586
Why would you bribe him?

34:06.669 --> 34:12.050
To expand this hospital
and save as many lives as possible.

34:12.592 --> 34:15.053
I will do whatever it takes
for that cause.

34:17.388 --> 34:20.308
Doing that, the future of
Japanese healthcare will be--

34:20.391 --> 34:25.104
I have seen countless hospitals collapse
because of that kind of idealistic talk.

34:27.857 --> 34:32.445
Saving as many lives
as possible through politics…

34:34.614 --> 34:36.866
That may just be idealistic talk.

34:39.494 --> 34:43.081
I might drag you into this as well.

34:43.831 --> 34:45.249
If you want out, do it now.

34:50.046 --> 34:52.548
I will give it some thought.

34:56.928 --> 34:58.846
The bribes were always in cash.

35:00.264 --> 35:01.224
And that day,

35:01.724 --> 35:07.188
we tracked down their location
and were about to secure the evidence,

35:08.106 --> 35:11.025
but Kakei caught wind of our movements.

35:11.109 --> 35:12.276
Follow him!

35:12.944 --> 35:13.903
Okay!

35:15.988 --> 35:17.156
Mr. Kakei!

35:20.118 --> 35:21.202
What?

35:24.455 --> 35:25.623
I…

35:28.334 --> 35:31.504
I believe the role of politics
is to create a world

35:33.005 --> 35:35.007
where we can call what is right, right.

35:49.105 --> 35:50.857
Aota's bill

35:52.108 --> 35:54.652
is going through
the internal procedures, right?

35:55.820 --> 35:57.655
You want it to pass, don't you?

36:00.116 --> 36:01.909
You were being threatened?

36:03.786 --> 36:05.413
Neither I nor Kakei

36:07.206 --> 36:10.168
knew the truth behind Mr. Aota's death.

36:14.380 --> 36:15.548
So,

36:17.091 --> 36:20.011
when Kakei found out that Mr. Aota
was going to be autopsied,

36:21.470 --> 36:22.972
he panicked…

36:25.850 --> 36:26.767
and he…

36:26.851 --> 36:28.811
You didn't have to…

36:33.024 --> 36:34.525
That bill…

36:37.236 --> 36:39.780
contained all of Mr. Aota's hopes.

36:44.410 --> 36:46.287
I don't understand.

36:47.955 --> 36:52.627
I don't understand why you've kept quiet
this whole time, Kaede.

36:53.669 --> 36:57.173
After all, you weren't the one
who fabricated the evidence, right?

36:57.924 --> 37:00.343
You're still hiding something, aren't you?

37:04.597 --> 37:05.973
A prosecutor came.

37:06.849 --> 37:07.934
A prosecutor?

37:14.482 --> 37:17.777
He told me that if he were transported
to the hospital as he was,

37:18.444 --> 37:21.489
it would be written off
as a disease or sudden death.

37:23.115 --> 37:26.077
He said everything
would be covered up by Kakei.

37:28.621 --> 37:31.207
The corruption my husband tried to expose,

37:32.124 --> 37:33.876
and the hopes he had in politics,

37:33.960 --> 37:36.587
would all be wiped away
as if they never happened.

37:38.631 --> 37:41.133
I absolutely could not allow that.

37:43.886 --> 37:46.264
So, I decided to wager everything on this.

37:47.723 --> 37:48.766
But…

37:50.476 --> 37:53.396
I've been worried this entire time
if it was the right thing to do.

37:55.106 --> 37:59.944
The next day, when the police contacted me
saying they found him hanging,

38:01.570 --> 38:04.115
it completely stopped making sense to me.

38:29.849 --> 38:32.351
Oh, it's very red.

38:32.435 --> 38:33.728
Let's see.

38:33.811 --> 38:34.645
There.

38:36.355 --> 38:37.982
Oh, that was shocking.

38:38.065 --> 38:39.859
Sorry, that's not why I'm here.

38:39.942 --> 38:42.236
I didn't do that on purpose, sorry.

38:42.320 --> 38:44.113
Oh, man.

38:45.197 --> 38:46.365
Mizusawa.

38:47.074 --> 38:48.200
That's you, right?

38:48.284 --> 38:50.786
What was the conclusion
on Aota's cause of death?

38:52.705 --> 38:54.707
It's believed to be tension pneumothorax

38:54.790 --> 38:56.917
resulting from a fall down the stairs.

38:57.001 --> 39:00.296
Is there a possibility that someone
intentionally pushed him down?

39:01.047 --> 39:04.133
None of the wounds
or bruises left on Mr. Aota's body

39:04.216 --> 39:06.969
provides clear proof of homicidal intent.

39:07.053 --> 39:10.306
Furthermore, considering their statements,
it doesn't add up.

39:11.015 --> 39:12.266
It doesn't add up, huh?

39:12.350 --> 39:13.434
Yes.

39:13.517 --> 39:14.560
It doesn't add up.

39:14.643 --> 39:19.106
It doesn't add up, which means
it was bribery after all.

39:19.190 --> 39:20.358
Oops.

39:20.441 --> 39:22.360
Tails, that makes sense.

39:22.443 --> 39:25.196
Excuse me, but who are you?

39:26.781 --> 39:27.948
I'm Ota.

39:28.532 --> 39:30.284
From the Public Prosecutors Office.

39:32.119 --> 39:33.496
A prosecutor?

39:33.579 --> 39:36.415
By the way,
I heard you went to see Dr. Kujo?

39:37.041 --> 39:38.042
How did it go?

39:38.125 --> 39:39.960
Were you able to speak with him?

39:43.297 --> 39:44.340
Well?

39:47.301 --> 39:48.636
You didn't?

39:48.719 --> 39:49.762
Oh, listen.

39:49.845 --> 39:54.850
Bribery paid in cash makes it
quite difficult to secure evidence.

39:55.768 --> 39:59.563
However, it has been confirmed
that Chairman Mukai

39:59.647 --> 40:01.273
was at the hotel that day.

40:01.816 --> 40:05.528
Therefore, if we have
Mr. Aota's autopsy results

40:06.487 --> 40:08.614
and the testimony of both individuals,

40:09.115 --> 40:12.535
it will serve as major leverage
to pursue Kakei.

40:12.618 --> 40:14.328
Your methods are foul.

40:15.246 --> 40:18.791
Our objective is also
to uncover the truth.

40:18.874 --> 40:21.752
An unnatural death
must always be autopsied.

40:21.836 --> 40:25.881
You just used the MEJ system
to bring down a powerful politician.

40:26.549 --> 40:27.383
Used?

40:27.466 --> 40:29.343
Fabricating a suicide by hanging

40:29.427 --> 40:32.138
constitutes the crimes
of damaging and abandoning a corpse.

40:34.473 --> 40:35.766
Is that so?

40:36.976 --> 40:38.060
What?

40:41.021 --> 40:42.314
Please leave.

40:45.276 --> 40:48.863
This is a place
to listen to the voices of the deceased

40:48.946 --> 40:51.282
and uncover the truth.

40:53.534 --> 40:58.205
It is a place to learn
what they loved and who loved them.

40:59.248 --> 41:01.917
It's not for you to bring in
your self-serving narratives!

41:19.518 --> 41:20.936
Didn't you hear her?

41:21.687 --> 41:22.855
Please leave.

41:30.321 --> 41:32.448
Heads or tails? Pick.

41:39.413 --> 41:40.414
What?

41:44.668 --> 41:47.421
See you around.

42:02.311 --> 42:04.855
I think I went a bit too far.

42:08.192 --> 42:10.903
You can just be scolded for it later.

42:12.321 --> 42:13.572
Don't worry about it.

42:46.272 --> 42:52.945
I still want… to live in a world
where I can call what is right, right.

42:55.239 --> 42:56.073
Yeah.

42:58.534 --> 43:01.287
You can't let people
you don't even believe are right

43:01.787 --> 43:03.831
run your life.

43:10.588 --> 43:12.464
Reading the room

43:13.132 --> 43:15.593
is different from
letting yourself be used.

43:20.723 --> 43:21.849
You're right.

43:31.317 --> 43:34.069
So Kakei ended up
not being prosecuted after all, huh?

43:34.737 --> 43:37.323
They say he claims
his secretary did everything.

43:38.407 --> 43:40.826
In the end, nothing changes, huh?

43:42.953 --> 43:44.913
It looks like the bill Mr. Aota drafted

43:46.081 --> 43:48.125
was properly submitted.

43:49.209 --> 43:51.837
The younger politicians
carried on his vision.

43:51.920 --> 43:53.339
It's true!

43:54.089 --> 43:56.425
If you seriously want to change things,

43:56.508 --> 43:57.968
they will change.

43:59.303 --> 44:01.096
I want to believe that.

44:05.392 --> 44:07.436
All right, let's work.

44:22.993 --> 44:25.871
Subtitle translation by: Maslin F.
